---
// The test builder, in the docs layout: its own tab in the header, with the guides on writing tests beside it.
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import TestBuilder from '../components/TestBuilder/index.jsx';
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Test builder',
		description: 'Pick the attributes of a Maester test, with the rubric for each one, and get the code.',
		tableOfContents: false,
		// A tool, not a page in a sequence: no previous and next links under it.
		prev: false,
		next: false,
	}}
>
	<p>
		Every Maester test declares what it is about, how urgent a failure is and what it needs to run, in a <code>[MaesterTest()]</code> attribute. Pick the values here and the code updates as you go. The help button beside a field opens what it means and the rule reviewers apply.
	</p>
	<p>
		The lists and rules on this page are generated from the files Maester itself uses, so they match what the unit tests and the review step enforce. The full text is in the <a href="/docs/writing-tests/attribute-rubric">attribute rubric</a>.
	</p>
	<div class="not-content">
		<TestBuilder client:load />
	</div>
</StarlightPage>
